But I used to play an online site for nethack!  You would telnet there and
login as "nethack" or something like that and it would allow you to play.  
It has been a long time and I have since lost the address (and I don't even
know if it would still be running).  

The advantage of a nethack that you can telnet to is that you immediately
start competing with everyone else in net-land.  The top 100 list would most
certainly turn into an exciting battle...

As for setting one up, it would be pretty easy.  You just need lots of CPU
for when all the nethack people start logging into the system.  

